Provisioning of github-mcp-server
----------------------------------
The github-mcp-server binary itself is intentionally NOT tracked in git (it is
a ~13 MB third-party binary and is excluded by .gitignore). The repository ships
only its MIT LICENSE and README under .mcp/. A fresh clone therefore does not
contain the executable.

There is currently no automated provisioning step in this repository (no Ansible
task, install script, Makefile target, or package.json hook) that downloads or
builds .mcp/github-mcp-server. The runtime expects it at the path referenced by
.mcp/config.json (`${AUTOBOT_PROJECT_ROOT:-/opt/autobot/code_source}/.mcp/
github-mcp-server`) and the integration test invokes `./github-mcp-server stdio`
(autobot-infrastructure/shared/scripts/test_mcp_integration.sh), but neither
fetches it.

Until an automated fetch is added, the binary must be obtained out-of-band from
the upstream project — download the appropriate release asset, or build from
source — and placed at .mcp/github-mcp-server:

  Releases: https://github.com/github/github-mcp-server/releases
  Source:   https://github.com/github/github-mcp-server

(Adding an automated, checksum-verified provisioning step is tracked as a
follow-up; see the repository issue tracker.)
